---
layout: changelog
title: "Send email and SMS through Bird with Appwrite Messaging"
date: 2026-11-25
cover: /images/blog/announcing-bird-messaging-providers/cover.avif
tags: messaging, auth, console, integrations
---

Appwrite Messaging has two new providers for [Bird](https://bird.com). The [Bird email provider](/docs/products/messaging/bird-email) sends through Bird's HTTP email API, and the [Bird SMS provider](/docs/products/messaging/bird-sms) sends from a number or sender ID your Bird workspace owns. Both take a Bird API key.

On Appwrite Cloud, click **Connect with Bird** on either provider and Appwrite creates a key with only `emails:write` or `sms:write`, then fills in the provider for you. The project **Settings** > **SMTP** tab has a Bird tile too, which sets up [custom SMTP](/docs/products/auth/message-templates#smtp-one-click-setup) through Bird's regional relay.

